in{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=3.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+C \\\\ 3 & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ 3 & =-2\\cdot 0+C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =3-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =3-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =3-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $5\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}.$" 13194139534468 true] [17592186289948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289949 13194139534468 true] [17592186289948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289950 13194139534468 true] [17592186289948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289951 13194139534468 true] [17592186289948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289952 13194139534468 true] [17592186289948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289953 13194139534468 true] [17592186289948 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534468 true] [17592186289948 1041 "selection" 13194139534468 true] [17592186289948 1104 #edb/ref 17592186289950 13194139534468 true] [17592186289948 1110 #uuid "62cdb047-288d-5b95-82e5-eb922356d91f" 13194139534468 true] [17592186289949 1034 "4\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}" 13194139534468 true] [17592186289949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534468 true] [17592186289949 1111 #uuid "cecfbe4f-d6cd-574b-a887-60c20f75af65" 13194139534468 true] [17592186289950 1034 "5\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}" 13194139534468 true] [17592186289950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534468 true] [17592186289950